---
description: API Implementation Workflow
alwaysApply: false
---

### Repository

- Implement efficient database queries with LIMIT/OFFSET
- Use database indexes for search fields
- Consider caching for frequently accessed data
- Optimize queries to avoid N+1 problems
- Set reasonable default limits

### Handler

All protected endpoints must use `middleware.AuthMiddleware(firebaseAuth)`.

If new API is not specified whether authentication is required (whether API is protected or not), ask the user.

All request path and query params must be validated:

- Check pagination bounds (page >= 1, limit 1-100)
- Validate search query length and content
- Ensure proper error messages for validation failures
- Handle edge cases (empty results, invalid parameters)

MUST write unit test. Refer to "Writing unit tests" rules.

### Documentation

Documentation MUST be updated accordingly.
